   "body": "## Goal\nPrepare a prospective design supplement for attempt selection and stopping over the existing paired plan and lossless attempt envelope. Expected gain: benchmark/baseline/attempt-policy-0148.md and .json give the next independent reviewer a deterministic, source-pinned contract for finite scheduling, failures, extra attempts and stopping, without selecting favorable responses. The gap is already measured in benchmark/attempt-evidence-0143.md (Accounting and controls): multiple attempts produce zero completion and no retry/selection/stopping policy is authorized. Do not repeat that gap survey. This design authorizes no executions and changes no existing accounting. No session can run LabVIEW.\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Check .session/exports/manifest.json and report #678 availability. Pin starting commit/tree and source hashes. Read the governing evaluation baseline requirements, existing runner contract, precision design and relevant attempt-envelope/paired-plan contracts. Report the documented boundary before proposing the supplement. #678 closes F2 only; do not repeat its probes.\n- [ ] Define a separately versioned prospective policy referencing immutable manifest/plan/settings identities and existing case/pair/repetition/arm/slot/attempt identities. Reuse explicit per-arm repetition mappings and existing arm ordering. Define required preflight fields, finite scheduling order, terminal states, completion and failure accounting, stopping causes and the treatment of missing/unstarted slots. Preserve all attempts and their byte evidence; never impute an arm, discard an unfavorable attempt or turn a transport success into semantic credit.\n- [ ] Use a conservative no-automatic-retry policy for this first version. Specify deterministic handling of a failed/interrupted/unsupported/empty/invalid attempt, duplicate submissions, unsolicited extra attempts, missing evidence, mismatched settings, budget exhaustion and hard evidence/resource failure. Distingui